  "body": "Fixes #6536. save.sh now encrypts to a temp file in the same directory, verifies it is non-empty and decrypts back to exactly the plaintext state (which also proves lineage, mirroring plan.sh), preserves the existing .enc mode, and atomically renames it over terraform.tfstate.enc. A failed or interrupted sops run leaves the previous .enc byte-identical; the EXIT trap removes the temp file and the .lock exactly as before. Adds infra/dns/test_save_atomic.sh (stub identity-cipher sops; oracle: the previous .enc is the record): failing -e leaves .enc unchanged with non-zero exit and no temp/lock residue, succeeding -e installs the new ciphertext, already-current fast path still skips re-encryption - 9/9 checks pass on the laptop. load.sh assessment (recorded on #6536): its in-place decrypt write is safe-by-reconstruction - the plaintext target is fully re-derivable from the intact .enc, so a truncated plaintext is recovered by re-running load; it is documented rather than changed. Shellcheck reports only pre-existing style findings for save.sh. Queue task 14343, lane code-h.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796813451&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=8021&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F8021&signature=5ce4d184d23afc3b21227dec3305b0ddc5006df7e1cda348d88bcd9db829e0ed\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/code